  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_018, acc 0.619) uses pca_n2000 as the RNA encoder, and RNA is clearly the dominant signal (image_only acc 0.208 vs rna_only 0.485). All six completed experiments use pca_n2000, so we have zero evidence about whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) could extract a superior RNA representation. Question: config_030 changes exactly one variable from config_018—swapping pca_n2000 for scvi_n200 while keeping multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, and concat fixed—directly isolating the effect of RNA representation quality in the best-performing pipeline. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA modality drives most of the predictive signal, so improving its encoder has the highest potential leverage. A single-variable A/B against the current best cleanly attributes any performance shift to the encoder choice, and the answer reshapes the entire remaining search (if scvi helps, we prioritize it across all subsequent configs; if it doesn't, we can rule it out and focus budget on image encoder or fusion strategy)."
}

